"""On request, 2026-09-24: the Telugu consent forms for one clinic.

The clinic signed up with batchusantosh@gmail.com and asked for the Telugu
pages of the Dental Surgeons Association consent book, the same book the
English starter forms (domains/consent/starter_templates.py) came from. Those
pages are images in the PDF, so the text below was transcribed by hand.

Isolated on purpose: one clinic, one request, not a product default. Delete
this file once it has run.

Edited like the English starters, so both sets read the same way on the
rendered form:
- The name, signature and date lines are dropped: the renderer draws them.
- Blanks written for a pen ("డాక్టర్ ......") are reworded to point at the
  dentist named on the form, as the English versions do.
- Stray characters from the booklet's typesetting are cleaned up.
Otherwise the wording is the booklet's own, including the root canal list,
which has nine items in Telugu where the English has ten (no perforation line).

Standalone, so it can be piped into the backend container without a deploy:
    docker exec -i molarplus-backend-1 python - --email X [--apply] < this_file
Dry run unless --apply. Skips any form whose name the clinic already has.
"""
